@startuml
title Private mint — CMTATAztec

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 250

actor "Minter\n(the issuer)" as Minter
box "Client side — proved on the minter's device" #F4F8FC
participant "mint(to, amount)\nexternal private" as Priv
end box
database "Public state" as PS
box "Sequencer — public" #FDF4F4
participant "_mint(caller, amount)\nexternal public, only_self" as Pub
end box
participant "Issuer" as Issuer
participant "Recipient" as To

Minter -> Priv : mint(to, amount)
note right of Priv
  No authwit. Minting is authorised by a role, not by
  the recipient, so there is nothing for `to` to sign.
end note

Priv -> PS : read issuer_address
Priv -> PS : read is_frozen(to)
note over Priv, PS
  Only the freeze flag is checked. The blacklist and whitelist
  are NOT applied to mint: operateOnTransfer runs on transfer only.
end note

Priv -> To : new note for `to`, onchain_constrained
Priv -> Issuer : copy of that note, offchain

Priv -> Pub : enqueue_self _mint(msg_sender(), amount)
note over Pub
  What becomes public here: the MINTER's address and the amount.
  The recipient `to` is never passed across, so who received the
  tokens stays private. The amount is public either way, because
  total_supply is public and moves by exactly that much.
end note
Pub -> PS : only_role(MINTER_ROLE, caller)
Pub -> PS : assert not paused
Pub -> PS : total_supply += amount

@enduml
